ay Embeddings:** Daily temporal patterns (288 × temp_dim_tid)\n- **Day-of-Week Embeddings:** Weekly patterns (7 × temp_dim_diw)\n- **Feature Embeddings:** Time series features via Conv2d\n\n#### 2. **Temporal Search Layer (NAS Component)**\nCandidate Operators:\n- **DCC_2:** Dilated Causal Convolution with dilation=2\n- **Informer:** ProbSparse attention mechanism for efficient long-range modeling\n\nArchitecture:\n- DAG structure with 4 search nodes (default)\n- Mixed operations with learnable architecture weights\n- Mode: ONE_PATH_FIXED (uses argmax for inference)\n\n#### 3. **Multi-Patch Transfer Module**\n- Multi-scale temporal processing\n- Scale list: [1, 2, 3] (configurable)\n- Compresses temporal representations at different scales\n- Uses lightweight linear layers (LightLinear)\n\n#### 4. **Spatial Search Layer (NAS Component)**\nCandidate Operators:\n- **GNN_fixed:** Graph convolution with fixed adjacency matrix\n- **GNN_adap:** Adaptive graph convolution with learned adjacency\n- **GNN_att:** Graph attention using LinearFormer\n\nArchitecture:\n- Multi-scale DAG structure (one DAG per scale)\n- Separate architecture parameters for each scale\n- Combines multi-scale spatial representations\n\n#### 5. **Output Layers**\n- Spatial fusion: Combines multi-scale features\n- End convolution: 2-layer MLP with ReLU\n- Final projection to (output_window × output_dim)\n\n---\n\n## Key Transformations from Original to LibCity\n\n### 1. **Data Format Conversion**\n**Original Format:** `[B, C, N, T]`\n**LibCity Format:** `[B, T, N, C]`\n\n**Handling:**\n```python\n# Input conversion in forward()\ninputs = batch[\'X\']  # [B, T, N, C]\ninputs = x.permute(0, 3, 2, 1)  # [B, C, N, T] for internal processing\n\n# Output conversion\nx = x.view(batch_size, self.output_window, num_nodes, self.output_dim)  # [B, T_out, N, C_out]\n```\n\n### 2. **Base Class Inheritance**\n**Original:** `nn.Module`\n**LibCity:** `AbstractTrafficStateModel`\n\n**Required Methods:**\n- `__init__(config, data_feature)` - Initialize from LibCity config\n- `forward(batch)` - Process batch dict with \'X\' key\n- `predict(batch)` - Return predictions\n- `calculate_loss(batch)` - Compute masked MAE loss\n\n### 3. **Configuration Adaptation**\n**Original:** Custom YAML config with nested structure\n**LibCity:** Flat JSON config with standard keys\n\n**Mapping:**\n```python\n# Original config.model.hidden_channels → LibCity config[\'hidden_channels\']\n# Original config.data.num_sensors → LibCity data_feature[\'num_nodes\']\n# Original config.data.in_length → LibCity config[\'input_window\']\n```\n\n### 4. **Adjacency Matrix Handling**\n**Original:** Passed directly to model constructor\n**LibCity:** Retrieved from data_feature dict\n\n**Implementation:**\n```python\ndef _build_adjacency_matrix(self, data_feature):\n    adj_mx = data_feature.get(\'adj_mx\')\n    if adj_mx is not None:\n        # Normalize using asymmetric normalization\n        adj_mx = self._asym_adj(adj_mx)\n    else:\n        # Fallback to identity matrix\n        adj_mx = np.eye(self.num_nodes)\n    return adj_mx\n```\n\n### 5. **NAS Mode Simplification**\n**Original:** Full NAS training with architecture search\n**LibCity:** Fixed architecture mode (ONE_PATH_FIXED)\n\n**Rationale:**\n- Focuses on inference capability\n- Uses argmax of learned architecture weights\n- Simplifies training (no need for separate architecture optimizer)\n- Can still load pre-searched architectures\n\n**Implementation:**\n```python\n# Set mode in __init__\nself.set_mode(Mode.ONE_PATH_FIXED)\n\n# In MixedOp\nif mode == Mode.ONE_PATH_FIXED:\n    probs = F.softmax(self._candidate_alphas.data, dim=0)\n    op = torch.argmax(probs).item()\n    self._sample_idx = np.array([op], dtype=np.int32)\n```\n\n### 6. **Loss Function**\n**Original:** Custom loss with optional regularization\n**LibCity:** Standard masked MAE\n\n```python\ndef calculate_loss(self, batch):\n    y_true = batch[\'y\']\n    y_predicted = self.predict(batch)\n    y_true = self._scaler.inverse_transform(y_true[..., :self.output_dim])\n    y_predicted = self._scaler.inverse_transform(y_predicted[..., :self.output_dim])\n    return loss.masked_mae_torch(y_predicted, y_true, 0)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Configuration Parameters\n\n### Model Architecture\n```json\n{\n  "hidden_channels": 32,           // Hidden dimension for graph convolutions\n  "end_channels": 512,              // Final MLP hidden dimension\n  "scale_list": [1, 2, 3],         // Multi-scale temporal processing\n}\n```\n\n### Neural Architecture Search\n```json\n{\n  "layer_names": ["TemporalSearch", "SpatialSearch"],\n  "temporal_operations": ["DCC_2", "Informer"],\n  "spatial_operations": ["GNN_fixed", "GNN_adap", "GNN_att"],\n  "num_temporal_search_node": 4,   // DAG nodes for temporal search\n  "num_spatial_search_node": 4,    // DAG nodes for spatial search\n}\n```\n\n### Graph Neural Network\n```json\n{\n  "num_hop": 1,                     // K-order diffusion steps\n  "num_att_layers": 1,              // LinearFormer layers for GNN_att\n}\n```\n\n### Linear Layers\n```json\n{\n  "IsUseLinear": true,              // Enable LightLinear module\n  "num_linear_layers": 3,           // Stacked lightweight layers\n  "num_mlp_layers": 3,              // MLP encoder layers\n}\n```\n\n### Embeddings\n```json\n{\n  "mlp_node_dim": 32,               // Node embedding dimension\n  "temp_dim_tid": 32,               // Time-of-day embedding dimension\n  "temp_dim_diw": 32,               // Day-of-week embedding dimension\n  "time_of_day_size": 288,          // Number of time slots per day (5 min intervals)\n  "day_of_week_size": 7,            // Days per week\n}\n```\n\n### Training\n```json\n{\n  "input_window": 12,\n  "output_window": 12,\n  "learning_rate": 0.001,\n  "weight_decay": 0.0001,\n  "max_epoch": 100,\n  "lr_decay": true,\n  "lr_decay_ratio": 0.1,\n  "milestones": [50, 60, 70, 80],\n  "clip_grad_norm": true,\n  "max_grad_norm": 5,\n  "use_early_stop": true,\n  "patience": 30\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Operator Details\n\n### Temporal Operators\n\n#### 1. DCC (Dilated Causal Convolution)\n```python\nclass DCCLayer(nn.Module):\n    # Gated Temporal Unit with causal padding\n    # filter = tanh(CausalConv(x))\n    # gate = sigmoid(CausalConv(x))\n    # output = filter * gate\n```\n\n#### 2. Informer\n```python\nclass InformerLayer(nn.Module):\n    # ProbSparse Attention for efficient long-range modeling\n    # Reduces complexity from O(L^2) to O(L log L)\n    # Query sparsity measurement and top-k selection\n```\n\n### Spatial Operators\n\n#### 1. GNN_fixed\n```python\nclass GNN_fixed(nn.Module):\n    # K-order graph convolution with fixed adjacency\n    # Outputs = [x, A@x, A^2@x, ..., A^K@x]\n    # Linear fusion of multi-hop features\n```\n\n#### 2. GNN_adap\n```python\nclass GNN_adap(nn.Module):\n    # Adaptive adjacency: A_adap = softmax(ReLU(E1 @ E2))\n    # E1, E2 are learnable node embeddings\n    # Masked softmax to preserve sparsity patterns\n```\n\n#### 3. GNN_att\n```python\nclass GNN_att(nn.Module):\n    # LinearFormer-based graph attention\n    # Efficient linear attention with learned positional encoding\n    # Multi-layer transformer architecture\n```\n\n---\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### 1. **Fixed Architecture Mode**\n- **Decision:** Use ONE_PATH_FIXED mode by default\n- **Rationale:**\n  - Simplifies initial migration and testing\n  - Avoids complexity of dual optimizer setup\n  - Can still demonstrate NAS capability\n  - Pre-searched architectures can be loaded\n- **Future Work:** Add full NAS training support with architecture search loop\n\n### 2. **Adjacency Matrix Fallback**\n- **Decision:** Use identity matrix if no adjacency provided\n- **Rationale:**\n  - Ensures model runs on any dataset\n  - GNN_adap can learn graph structure\n  - GNN_att doesn\'t require fixed adjacency\n- **Warning:** Logged when using fallback\n\n### 3. **Temporal Feature Handling**\n- **Decision:** Auto-detect available temporal features from feature_dim\n- **Mapping:**\n  - `feature_dim == 1` → No temporal features\n  - `feature_dim == 2` → Time-of-day only\n  - `feature_dim == 3` → Time-of-day + day-of-week\n- **Benefit:** Flexible dataset compatibility\n\n### 4. **Multi-Scale Processing**\n- **Decision:** Keep 3-scale default (scale_list=[1,2,3])\n- **Rationale:**\n  - Captures patterns at different temporal granularities\n  - Balances model capacity and efficiency\n- **Configurable:** Can adjust via config\n\n### 5. **Operator Preservation**\n- **Decision:** Implement all original operators without simplification\n- **Rationale:**\n  - Maintains model expressiveness\n  - Enables fair comparison with original implementation\n  - Preserves NAS search space\n\n---\n\n## Testing Checklist\n\n### Basic Functionality\n- [ ] Import test: `from libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction import AutoSTF`\n- [ ] Instantiation: `model = AutoSTF(config, data_feature)`\n- [ ] Forward pass: `output = model(batch)`\n- [ ] Loss computation: `loss = model.calculate_loss(batch)`\n\n### Shape Verification\n- [ ] Input: `batch[\'X\']` shape `[B, T_in, N, C]`\n- [ ] Output: shape `[B, T_out, N, C_out]`\n- [ ] Embeddings: Correct dimensions\n- [ ] Intermediate tensors: Valid shapes through pipeline\n\n### Component Tests\n- [ ] Temporal search layer: Processes `[B, C, N, T]` correctly\n- [ ] Spatial search layer: Handles multi-scale inputs\n- [ ] Mixed operations: Selects operators based on mode\n- [ ] Graph convolutions: Work with adjacency matrix\n\n### Integration Tests\n- [ ] LibCity executor compatibility\n- [ ] Data loader integration\n- [ ] Scaler inverse transform\n- [ ] Multi-GPU support (if applicable)\n\n### Edge Cases\n- [ ] No adjacency matrix provided (identity fallback)\n- [ ] Single feature (feature_dim=1)\n- [ ] Different input/output windows\n- [ ] Various batch sizes\n\n---\n\n## Known Limitations\n\n### 1. **Full NAS Training Not Supported**\n- Current implementation uses fixed architecture mode\n- Architecture search loop requires custom executor\n- Can be added as future enhancement\n\n### 2. **Architecture Weight Initialization**\n- Architecture parameters initialized to zeros\n- May need pre-trained weights for optimal performance\n- Random initialization may work but suboptimal\n\n### 3. **Memory Requirements**\n- Model has significant memory footprint due to:\n  - Multiple candidate operators\n  - Multi-scale processing\n  - Large embedding dimensions\n- May need gradient checkpointing for very large graphs\n\n### 4. **Dataset-Specific Tuning**\n- Default config based on PEMS04\n- May need adjustment for different:\n  - Graph sizes (num_nodes)\n  - Temporal resolutions (time_of_day_size)\n  - Feature compositions\n\n---\n\n## Usage Example\n\n### Basic Training\n```python\nfrom libcity.pipeline import run_model\n\n# Using default config\nrun_model(\n    task=\'traffic_state_pred\',\n    model=\'AutoSTF\',\n    dataset=\'METR_LA\',\n    config_file=None  # Uses default AutoSTF.json\n)\n```\n\n### Custom Configuration\n```python\nrun_model(\n    task=\'traffic_state_pred\',\n    model=\'AutoSTF\',\n    dataset=\'PEMS_BAY\',\n    config_file=\'custom_autostf_config.json\'\n)\n```\n\n### Custom Config Example\n```json\n{\n  "hidden_channels": 64,\n  "end_channels": 1024,\n  "num_temporal_search_node": 6,\n  "num_spatial_search_node": 6,\n  "learning_rate": 0.0005,\n  "max_epoch": 150\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Performance Expectations\n\n### Model Capacity\n- **Parameters:** ~1-5M (depending on num_nodes and hidden_channels)\n- **Operators:** 5 total (2 temporal + 3 spatial)\n- **Search Space:** Exponential in number of DAG nodes\n\n### Computational Complexity\n- **Temporal:** O(T × N × C²) for DCC, O(T log T × N × C²) for Informer\n- **Spatial:** O(N² × C²) for GNN operations\n- **Multi-Scale:** 3× due to scale_list length\n\n### Dataset Recommendations\n- **Small Graphs:** < 500 nodes (e.g., METR-LA: 207, PEMS-BAY: 325)\n- **Medium Graphs:** 500-1000 nodes (e.g., PEMS04: 307, PEMS08: 170)\n- **Large Graphs:** May need model simplification\n\n---\n\n## Future Enhancements\n\n### 1. **Full NAS Training Support**\n```python\n# Add architecture optimizer\narch_optimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.arch_parameters(), lr=config[\'arch_lr\'])\n\n# Alternating optimization loop\nfor epoch in epochs:\n    # Train architecture parameters\n    model.set_mode(Mode.TWO_PATHS)\n    arch_loss = model.calculate_loss(val_batch)\n    arch_optimizer.step()\n\n    # Train model weights\n    model.set_mode(Mode.ONE_PATH_RANDOM)\n    weight_loss = model.calculate_loss(train_batch)\n    weight_optimizer.step()\n```\n\n### 2. **Architecture Export/Import**\n```python\n# Export searched architecture\narch_params = {\n    \'temporal_alphas\': model.get_temporal_alphas(),\n    \'spatial_alphas\': model.get_spatial_alphas()\n}\ntorch.save(arch_params, \'searched_architecture.pt\')\n\n# Load pre-searched architecture\narch_params = torch.load(\'searched_architecture.pt\')\nmodel.set_arch_parameters(arch_params)\n```\n\n### 3. **Model Compression**\n- Discretize architecture (remove mixed operations)\n- Keep only selected operators\n- Reduce model size by ~60%\n\n### 4. **Enhanced Graph Learning**\n- Add graph structure learning module\n- Support dynamic adjacency matrices\n- Temporal graph evolution\n\n---\n\n## Citation\n\nIf using this model, please cite:\n\n```bibtex\n@inproceedings{autostf2023,\n  title={AutoSTF: Automated Spatio-Temporal Forecasting},\n  author={[Original Authors]},\n  booktitle={[Conference/Journal]},\n  year={2023}\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Contact\n\nFor issues or questions about this adaptation:\n- LibCity Framework: https://github.com/LibCity/Bigscity-LibCity\n- Original AutoSTF: https://github.com/HKUDS/AutoSTF\n\n---\n\n## Appendix: Complete File Structure\n\n```\nBigscity-LibCity/\n├── libcity/\n│   ├── model/\n│   │   └── traffic_speed_prediction/\n│   │       ├── AutoSTF.py                    # Main implementation (NEW)\n│